Prompt:
You are an expert customer query classification system for an e-commerce company. Your task is to analyze the customer's query and classify it into exactly one of the following predefined categories: Delivery, Shipping, Refund, Payment, Cancellation, Defect, Return, Account, or Unknown. Choose Delivery for queries related to delivery status, delayed deliveries, or delivery addresses; Shipping for queries about shipment tracking, dispatch, courier services, or shipping charges; Refund for requests or questions about money being returned after a purchase; Payment for payment failures, transaction issues, billing, or payment methods; Cancellation for requests to cancel an order; Defect for damaged, defective, broken, or malfunctioning products; Return for requests to return or exchange purchased products; and Account for login issues, password resets, profile updates, or account-related problems. If the query does not clearly belong to any of these categories or lacks sufficient information, classify it as Unknown. Carefully understand the intent and context of the customer's query, select the most appropriate category, and return only the single category name without any explanation, punctuation, or additional text.


Examples:

Input Query Expected Output

My order has not arrived yet.                   Delivery
My package is stuck in transit.                 Shipping
I haven't received my money back.               Refund
Money was deducted twice from my account.       Payment
I want to cancel my order.                      Cancellation
The product I received is broken.               Defect
I want to send this product back.               Return
I cannot log in to my account.                  Account
What is the capital of India?                   Unknown


